## Core Conventions

- Every page in `wiki/` has flat YAML frontmatter: `type`, `title`, `description`, `created`, `updated`, `tags`, `status` (minimum). Full schema: `~/.claude/skills/wiki/references/frontmatter.md`.
- `description` is one sentence about the page. Index entries are `- [[Page]] — <description>`, copied from it.
- Wikilinks use `[[Note Name]]`: filenames are unique across the vault, no paths needed.
- Never wikilink files in `.raw/`: Obsidian does not index dot-folders. Source pages keep the path to the original as a plain string in `url`.
- `.raw/` holds immutable source documents: never modify them.
- `wiki/index.md` is the master catalog, and `wiki/<folder>/_index.md` are sub-indexes: update them whenever a page is created, renamed or deleted.
- `wiki/log.md` is append-only. New entries go at the TOP.
- `wiki/hot.md` is a ~500-word cache of recent context: overwrite it completely after every operation.
- Contradictions between pages are marked with a `> [!contradiction]` callout on both pages. Knowledge gaps are marked with `> [!gap]`.
- Pages are written in {{LANGUAGE}}, in declarative present tense. Technical terms may stay in their original language.
- `reviewed: YYYY-MM-DD` means the owner checked the page. Claude sets it only when the owner says they checked the page ("I checked [[X]]"), never on its own. If `updated` is later than `reviewed`, the review is out of date.
- `stale_after: YYYY-MM-DD` marks pages with facts that expire on their own (prices, versions, current state, plans). From that date on the page is expired: say so when using it.
- Use `related` for cross-references between wiki pages and `sources` for the source pages a page is based on.
- Before `git push`, run `git pull --rebase`: the obsidian-git plugin may have committed to the same repository.

