## Operations

| Say | What happens |
|---|---|
| "ingest <file or URL>" | Source goes to `.raw/`, Claude writes a source page and updates every related page (`wiki-ingest`) |
| "query: <question>", "query deep: ..." | Answer from the wiki with citations (`wiki-query`) |
| "/save" | The current conversation becomes a wiki page (`save`) |
| "lint the wiki" | Health check: orphans, dead links, contradictions, gaps, expired and unreviewed pages (`wiki-lint`) |
| "I checked [[Page]]", "what needs review?" | Mark a page reviewed, or list what is worth checking (`wiki`) |
{{MODULE_OPERATIONS}}
## Status Values

- `seed`: exists, barely populated
- `developing`: has real content, not yet complete
- `mature`: comprehensive, well linked
- `evergreen`: unlikely to need updates

`status` is completeness, not trust: trust is `reviewed`, freshness is `stale_after`.
